 "text": "Brief reasoning for each question:\n\n1. **B.** A lack of insulin causes diabetes (বহুমূত্র).\n2. **C.** Sclerenchyma cells are dead, have thick lignified walls, and contain no chloroplasts.\n3. **C.** Reading the garbled matrix as |3 −4 2; −1 5 6; 7 −8 4|, the (1,2) cofactor is −[(−1)(4) − (6)(7)] = 46.\n4. **A.** CaCl₂ has a molar mass of 111, so 0.015 × 111 = 1.665 g/L, which is 1665 ppm.\n5. **B.** The distance from (2,3) to the line is |8 + 9 − 7|/5 = 2. The image point is twice that distance away, so 4 units.\n6. **A.** This is a guess. I believe the painter of \"The Five Senses\" is Rembrandt, who is not among the options.\n7. **D.** HI is the strongest hydrohalic acid.\n8. **B.** Bangladeshi textbooks usually give 4° as the limit; some sources say 5°.\n9. **C.** For a receding source, f′ = 120 × 320 / (320 + 15) ≈ 114.6 Hz.\n10. **C.** The period depends on the effective length. I read \"দোলনকার\" as a typo for \"দোলনকাল\".\n11. **C.** Atrial systole lasts about 0.1 s.\n12. **B.** This is a guess, because the objective function is missing from the question. The feasible region's corners are (0,0), (5,0), (4,2) and (0,4). An objective like 9x + 5y would give a maximum of 46 at (4,2).\n13. **C.** The average temperature is about 15 °C.\n14. **A.** l must be less than n, so l = 3 is impossible when n = 3.\n15. **D.** Radial, concentric and collateral are vascular bundle types; \"symmetric\" is not.\n\n{\"answers\": {\"67ab314c-5a13-4a89-b35f-6e9537e74c71-89189\": \"B\", \"68569189-0bf1-4a15-ae3f-60f829a88ebb-79778\": \"C\", \"6933878d-b2f3-4939-b07e-1ce5d40c908c-20187\": \"C\", \"6dac6d45-aa1a-4ca2-9137-ed74ad8d1311-71046\": \"A\", \"6ee561d5-27e9-47c7-a614-9752b1d8cc15-80683\": \"B\", \"71f25bf8-a76a-466d-bc74-007ef39e7c15-128717\": \"A\", \"72b547d4-bb13-45ee-98e7-16dc6fc75a49-44147\": \"D\", \"7365fff4-3ba8-4efb-ac67-5a7940463525-14949\": \"B\", \"752de91a-4a2e-4c17-b275-f73ebde26e01-59185\": \"C\", \"753d2e4a-c542-4740-b5ad-a0a57b2f1d35-81591\": \